---
// PRD PRV-04: Data Retention Policy & Telemetry Disclosure Page (Light Ribbon, AC-P14-07)
import '../styles/theme.css';
---
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
  <link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="/favicon.png" />
  <title>Data Retention & Privacy — Tether</title>
  <style>
    body {
      font-family: Inter, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif;
      margin: 0;
      padding: 3rem 1.5rem;
    }
    .container {
      max-width: 800px;
      margin: 0 auto;
    }
    h1 {
      font-size: 2.25rem;
    }
    h2 {
      color: var(--t-text-900);
      margin-top: 2rem;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--t-line);
      padding-bottom: 0.5rem;
    }
    p, li {
      color: var(--t-text-700);
      line-height: 1.6;
    }
    table {
      width: 100%;
      border-collapse: collapse;
      margin-top: 1rem;
      background: var(--t-surface);
      border: 1px solid var(--t-line);
      border-radius: 12px;
      overflow: hidden;
    }
    th, td {
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--t-line);
      padding: 0.75rem;
      text-align: left;
      color: var(--t-text-700);
    }
    th {
      background: var(--t-sunken);
      color: var(--t-text-900);
      font-weight: 600;
    }
    td strong {
      color: var(--t-text-900);
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <div class="container">
    <h1 class="hero-title">What the Relay Carries, Logs and Retains</h1>
    <p>Tether is built on a strict Zero-Plaintext-at-Rest guarantee (PRD PRV-03). The relay acts as an encrypted transport pipe and never inspects or persists cleartext web data.</p>

    <h2>Data Storage Inventory</h2>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Category</th>
          <th>What is Stored</th>
          <th>Retention</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>Page Content &amp; DOM</td>
          <td><strong>Nothing.</strong> Payloads are encrypted end-to-end via X25519 ECDH + AES-256-GCM.</td>
          <td>0 days</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Audit Trail</td>
          <td>Tool name, timestamp, tier, verdict (allow/deny), SHA-256 hash. <em>No URLs or argument values.</em></td>
          <td>30 days (default) / 0 days (self-host)</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Network Egress</td>
          <td>Registrable origin domain (e.g. <code>api.github.com</code>), timestamp, bytes transferred.</td>
          <td>30 days</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Credentials</td>
          <td>Client IDs, public keys, SHA-256 refresh token hashes. <em>No plaintext tokens or passwords.</em></td>
          <td>Until revoked</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2>Self-Host Parity (PRD FR-608)</h2>
    <p>In self-hosted deployments (<code>RELAY_MODE=selfhost</code>), metadata retention defaults to 0 days, ensuring zero long-term records are retained on external servers.</p>
  </div>
</body>
</html>
